#Unified Kill Chain

#Notes:

#Kill Chain – A term used to explain the various stages of an attack (og. Military)

#Threat modeling – A series of steps to ultimately improve the security of a system

#Asset – The technical term for a piece of software or hardware in IT

#Unified Kill Chain – Not a direct competitor to the Lockheed Martin cyber kill chain and MITRE’s ATT&CK, but rather a complement
  #Believes in 18 phases of attack:
    #Reconnaissance
    #Weaponization
    #Delivery
    #Social Engineering
    #Exploitation
    #Persistence
    #Defense Evasion
    #Command and Control
    #Pivoting
    #Discovery
    #Privilege Escalation
    #Execution
    #Credential Access
    #Lateral Movement
    #Collection
    #Exfiltration
    #Impact
    #Objectives

